      "worked_solution": "First, we can form a triangle by creating a vertical line from $A$ to the $x$-axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14216822/assets/3e5ebde9ee4132e0bd64cb2aaf2a3763abc2b0de1a798e87ed4ee652ca360078.png)\n\nUsing the tangent ratio, we have\n\n$$\n\\tan\\theta = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt 3} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt 3}{3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, using the inverse tangent, we get\n\n$$\n\\theta = \\arctan{\\left( \\dfrac{\\sqrt 3}{3} \\right)} = 30^\\circ.\n$$",
